#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:5
#: ead7bb1c4f034da297b36df451c8f9ea
msgid "Adding a new MAVLink Message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:7
#: ef57ce21466b47b3aaa95456abf7f073
msgid "Data and commands are passed between the ground station (i.e. Mission Planner, QGroundControl, MAVProxy, etc.) using the `MAVLink protocol <https://mavlink.io/en/>`__ over a serial interface. This page provides some high-level advice for adding a new MAVLink message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:11
#: 3bea37147c9e4c01bef3fce8bab8e31a
msgid "These instructions have only been tested on Linux (to be precise a VM running Ubuntu on a Windows machine). Instructions for setting up a VM are on the :ref:`SITL page <setting-up-sitl-on-windows>`. If you can run SITL, you should be able to follow the advice here. These instructions will not run natively on Windows or a Mac."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:17
#: 1953c3466cab43b5b41c3384f9886928
msgid "**Step #1:** Ensure you have the latest ArduPilot code installed. Also, check mavproxy. Mavproxy can be updated by running this command in a Terminal window:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:25
#: da493a0c489f47be8281ed33e2215895
msgid "**Step #2:** Decide what type of message you want to add and how it will fit in with the existing `MAVLink messages <https://mavlink.io/en/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:29
#: 5792480c710c4909a693f85c484a49b6
msgid "For example, you might want to send a new navigation command to the vehicle so that it can perform a trick (like a flip) in the middle of a mission (i.e. in AUTO mode).  In this case, you would need a new MAV_CMD_NAV_TRICK similar to the `MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT>`__  definition (search for \"MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT\" in the \\ `MAVLink messages <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html>`__ page)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:35
#: fa0355251b714218bbe011381039a25c
msgid "Alternatively, you may want to send down a new type of sensor data from the vehicle to the ground station.  Perhaps similar to the `SCALED_PRESSURE <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SCALED_PRESSURE>`__ message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:40
#: af24204064594e5ba8a50300f0e85b62
msgid "**Step #3:** Add the new message definition to the `common.xml <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/common.xml>`__ or `ardupilotmega.xml <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/ardupilotmega.xml>`__ file in the MAVLink submodule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:46
#: 30f0ba767e3f44c7b7d27bec8d9ebe52
msgid "If this command is generally useful, and will hopefully be added to the MAVLink protocol, then it should be added to the ../modules/mavlink/message_definitions/v1.0/common.xml file. If it is only for your personal use or only applicable to ArduPilot, then it should be added to the ardupilotmega.xml file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:51
#: eece249a10db4cb89881b8d7954ca8ef
msgid "**Step #4:** Add functions to the main vehicle code to handle sending or receiving the command to/from the ground station. A compile will be needed (ie. ./waf copter) to generate the MAVLink packet code so make sure to do that after editing the XML file. The MAVLink generation happens first, so it doesn't matter if the project compilation is successful or not due to other source code changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:53
#: 3bd062ff84b44a15837a5cc086c84965
msgid "The top-level of this code will most likely be in the vehicle's GCS_MAVLink_<vehicle>.cpp file (`GCS_MAVLink_Copter.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/GCS_MAVLink_Copter.cpp>`__ for ArduCopter) or in the `../libraries/GCS_MAVLink/GCS <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/GCS_MAVLink/GCS.h>`__ class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:59
#: 7746d285f8aa4f489f2c244f4920a2a6
msgid "In the first example where we want to add support for a new navigation command (i.e., a trick) the following would be required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:62
#: 75fd1064aec5488b81be35331e9c3365
msgid "Extend the `AP_Mission <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_Mission>`__ library's ``mission_cmd_to_mavlink()`` and ``mavlink_to_mission_cmd()`` functions to convert the MAVProxy command into an AP_Mission::Mission_Command structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:67
#: 7720d6137f03428cbda6dfd675d87cdb
msgid "Add a new case to the vehicle's commands_logic.cpp 's (`mode_auto.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_auto.cpp>`__ for ArduCopter) ``start_command()`` and ``verify_command()`` functions to check for the arrival of the new ``MAV_CMD_NAV_TRICK``. These should call two new functions that you create called ``do_trick()`` and ``verify_trick()`` (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:73
#: 39ce818ea9b2476196912d61724d9ece
msgid "Create these two new functions,  do_trick() and verify_trick(), that somehow command the vehicle *to perform the trick* (perhaps by calling another function in control_auto.cpp (`mode_auto.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_auto.cpp>`__ for ArduCopter) that sets the auto_mode variable and then calls a new ``auto_trick_start()`` function).  The ``do_trick()`` function will be called when the command is first invoked.  The ``verify_trick()`` will be called at 10hz (or higher) repeatedly until the trick is complete.  The ``verify_trick()`` function should return true when the trick has been completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:84
#: a059e620454744ea8e5c8fc34ffba73e
msgid "**Step #5:** Decide how you are going to handle the message at the GCS. One of the simplest ways is to use Mavproxy. MavProxy uses pymavlink to define the MAVLink messages, so you will need to rebuild pymavlink to include your custom message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:88
#: 404951b3478446528d985e5372a9d6cb
msgid "Remove the currently installed version of pymavlink. ``pip uninstall pymavlink``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:89
#: 3590c733365b4411a5219d247cf9e60e
msgid "Install the updated version. CD to ``ardupilot/modules/mavlink/pymavlink`` and run ``python3 setup.py install --user``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:91
#: f4e08d654a164712becba58c65755cbf
msgid "Mavproxy is now capable of sending or receiving the new message. To ask it to print out or send your message you need to implement a module. Modules are python plugins that allow you to add functionality to Mavproxy. By default on Ubuntu they are located in ``/usr/local/lib/python2.7/dist-packages/MAVProxy/modules/``. Here is an example of a module that prints the contents of a MY_CUSTOM_PACKET message. Look at the other modules for examples on how to trigger sending of messages using the command line interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:127
#: 3332ddcefc504913bf064e861c9d963b
msgid "If the message you added has an ID greater that 255 you will need to enable MAVLink 2 support. This can be done by setting the relevant ``SERIALn_PROTOCOL`` parameters (e.g. ``SERIAL1_PROTOCOL``) to 2 and starting Mavproxy with the ``--mav20`` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-mavlink-message.rst:130
#: 07f98683dcc24dff99dbbb6bca43c20c
msgid "**Step #6:** Consider contributing your code back to the main code base. Discuss this with other developers on `Discord <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ and/or :ref:`raise a pull request <submitting-patches-back-to-master>`. If you raise a pull request it is best to separate the change into at least two separate commits. One commit for the changes to the .xml files (i.e Step #3) and another for the changes to the vehicle code."
msgstr ""
